{"format":1,"manifest":{"name":"laravel-blade","publisher":"vyloxi","version":"1.0.0","displayName":"Laravel Blade Tools","description":"Format Blade and HTML together, tidy {{ }} spacing, switch {{ }} and {!! !!}, wrap in a directive, turn class attributes into @class, extract a component.","engines":{"ferrum":"^0.1.0"},"categories":["Tools"],"icon":"icon.png","repository":"https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market","license":"MIT","main":"extension.js","activationEvents":["onCommand:laravelBlade.format","onCommand:laravelBlade.tidyEchoes","onCommand:laravelBlade.toggleEcho","onCommand:laravelBlade.wrap","onCommand:laravelBlade.classDirective","onCommand:laravelBlade.extractComponent","onCommand:laravelBlade.extractPartial"],"permissions":["workspace.write"],"contributes":{"commands":[{"command":"laravelBlade.format","title":"Format Blade File","category":"Laravel Blade Tools"},{"command":"laravelBlade.tidyEchoes","title":"Tidy {{ }} Spacing","category":"Laravel Blade Tools"},{"command":"laravelBlade.toggleEcho","title":"Toggle {{ }} and {!! !!}","category":"Laravel Blade Tools"},{"command":"laravelBlade.wrap","title":"Wrap Selection in a Directive...","category":"Laravel Blade Tools"},{"command":"laravelBlade.classDirective","title":"Turn class=\"...\" into @class","category":"Laravel Blade Tools"},{"command":"laravelBlade.extractComponent","title":"Extract Selection to a Blade Component...","category":"Laravel Blade Tools"},{"command":"laravelBlade.extractPartial","title":"Extract Selection to a Partial (@include)...","category":"Laravel Blade Tools"}],"keybindings":[{"command":"laravelBlade.format","key":"Ctrl+Alt+B"}],"configuration":{"title":"Laravel Blade Tools","properties":{"laravelBlade.indentSize":{"type":"number","default":4,"description":"Spaces per indent level (1 to 8)."},"laravelBlade.useTabs":{"type":"boolean","default":false,"description":"Indent with tabs instead of spaces."},"laravelBlade.tidyEchoes":{"type":"boolean","default":true,"description":"Also put one space inside {{ }} and after @if, @foreach... when formatting."}}}}},"files":{"icon.png":{"encoding":"base64","content":""},"extension.js":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"// Laravel Blade: indent Blade and HTML together, tidy {{ }} spacing, switch {{ }} and {!! !!}, wrap a selection in a directive,\r\n// turn class attributes into @class, and pull markup out into a component or a partial.\r\n\r\nconst VOID = new Set(['area', 'base', 'br', 'col', 'embed', 'hr', 'img', 'input', 'link', 'meta', 'param', 'source', 'track', 'wbr']);\r\nconst RAW = new Set(['pre', 'textarea', 'script', 'style']);\r\n\r\nconst OPENERS = new Set(['if', 'foreach', 'forelse', 'for', 'while', 'unless', 'isset', 'auth', 'guest', 'can', 'cannot', 'canany', 'switch', 'push', 'pushonce', 'pushif', 'prepend', 'prependonce', 'error', 'env', 'production', 'once', 'verbatim', 'component', 'slot', 'fragment', 'session', 'hassection', 'sectionmissing', 'section', 'php', 'empty']);\r\nconst MIDDLE = new Set(['else', 'elseif', 'elsecan', 'elsecannot', 'elsecanany', 'elseauth', 'elseguest', 'elseenv', 'elseunless']);\r\nconst SECTION_ENDS = new Set(['show', 'stop', 'append', 'overwrite']);\r\n\r\n/** The tags and directives of one line, in the order they appear. Quoted text and {{ }} are blanked out first. */\r\nfunction tokens(line) {\r\n  const t = line.replace(/\\{\\{--[\\s\\S]*?--\\}\\}/g, '').replace(/\\{\\{[\\s\\S]*?\\}\\}|\\{!![\\s\\S]*?!!\\}/g, 'X').replace(/<!--[\\s\\S]*?-->/g, '').replace(/\"[^\"]*\"|'[^']*'/g, '\"\"');\r\n  const out = [];\r\n  for (const m of t.matchAll(/<(\\/?)([A-Za-z][\\w:.-]*)((?:[^<>]|\"\")*?)(\\/?)>/g)) {\r\n    const name = m[2].toLowerCase();\r\n    if (m[4] || VOID.has(name)) continue;\r\n    out.push({ i: m.index, k: m[1] ? 'tag-close' : 'tag-open', name });\r\n  }\r\n  for (const m of t.matchAll(/(?<![\\w@])@(end)?([A-Za-z]+)(\\s*\\()?/g)) {\r\n    const end = !!m[1];\r\n    const name = m[2].toLowerCase();\r\n    const paren = !!m[3];\r\n    if (end) {\r\n      if (OPENERS.has(name)) out.push({ i: m.index, k: 'd-close', name });\r\n    } else if (name === 'case' || name === 'default') out.push({ i: m.index, k: 'case' });\r\n    else if (MIDDLE.has(name)) out.push({ i: m.index, k: 'mid' });\r\n    else if (SECTION_ENDS.has(name)) out.push({ i: m.index, k: 'd-close', name: 'section' });\r\n    else if (name === 'empty') out.push({ i: m.index, k: paren ? 'd-open' : 'mid', name });\r\n    else if (name === 'php') {\r\n      if (!paren) out.push({ i: m.index, k: 'd-open', name });\r\n    } else if (name === 'section') {\r\n      const rest = t.slice(m.index);\r\n      const call = /^@section\\s*\\(([^)]*)\\)/i.exec(rest);\r\n      if (!(call && call[1].includes(','))) out.push({ i: m.index, k: 'd-open', name });\r\n    } else if (OPENERS.has(name)) out.push({ i: m.index, k: 'd-open', name });\r\n  }\r\n  return out.sort((a, b) => a.i - b.i);\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction popTo(stack, label) {\r\n  const at = stack.lastIndexOf(label);\r\n  if (at >= 0) stack.length = at;\r\n}\r\n\r\n/** Applies one line to the stack and returns the level the line is printed at. */\r\nfunction step(line, stack) {\r\n  let print = null;\r\n  const mark = () => {\r\n    if (print === null) print = stack.length;\r\n  };\r\n  for (const tok of tokens(line)) {\r\n    if (tok.k === 'tag-open') {\r\n      mark();\r\n      stack.push('<' + tok.name);\r\n    } else if (tok.k === 'd-open') {\r\n      mark();\r\n      stack.push('@' + tok.name);\r\n    } else if (tok.k === 'tag-close') {\r\n      popTo(stack, '<' + tok.name);\r\n      mark();\r\n    } else if (tok.k === 'd-close') {\r\n      if (stack[stack.length - 1] === '@case') stack.pop();\r\n      popTo(stack, '@' + (tok.name === 'forelse' ? 'forelse' : tok.name));\r\n      mark();\r\n    } else if (tok.k === 'mid') {\r\n      if (print === null) print = Math.max(0, stack.length - 1);\r\n    } else if (tok.k === 'case') {\r\n      if (stack[stack.length - 1] === '@case') stack.pop();\r\n      mark();\r\n      stack.push('@case');\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  return print === null ? stack.length : print;\r\n}\r\n\r\n/** Re-indents the whole text. Blank lines stay blank, and the inside of pre, textarea, script and style is left as it is. */\r\nfunction formatBlade(text, unit = '    ') {\r\n  const lines = text.replace(/\\r\\n/g, '\\n').split('\\n');\r\n  const stack = [];\r\n  let raw = null;\r\n  const out = [];\r\n  for (const original of lines) {\r\n    const t = original.trim();\r\n    if (raw) {\r\n      if (new RegExp('</' + raw + '\\\\s*>', 'i').test(t)) {\r\n        raw = null;\r\n        const level = step(t, stack);\r\n        out.push(unit.repeat(level) + t);\r\n      } else out.push(original);\r\n      continue;\r\n    }\r\n    if (!t) {\r\n      out.push('');\r\n      continue;\r\n    }\r\n    const before = stack.length;\r\n    const level = step(t, stack);\r\n    out.push(unit.repeat(level) + t);\r\n    for (const m of t.matchAll(/<(pre|textarea|script|style)\\b[^>]*>(?![\\s\\S]*<\\/\\1\\s*>)/gi)) {\r\n      if (!/\\/\\s*>$/.test(m[0])) raw = m[1].toLowerCase();\r\n    }\r\n    void before;\r\n  }\r\n  return out.join('\\n').replace(/\\n*$/, '\\n');\r\n}\r\n\r\n/** {{$x}} to {{ $x }}, {!!$x!!} to {!! $x !!}, and @if( to @if ( for the control directives. */\r\nfunction tidySpacing(text) {\r\n  return text\r\n    .replace(/\\{\\{(?!--)\\s*([^{}]*?)\\s*\\}\\}/g, (m, e) => '{{ ' + e + ' }}')\r\n    .replace(/\\{!!\\s*([^{}]*?)\\s*!!\\}/g, (m, e) => '{!! ' + e + ' !!}')\r\n    .replace(/@(if|elseif|foreach|forelse|for|while|unless|isset|can|cannot)\\(/g, '@$1 (');\r\n}\r\n\r\n/** Switches the echo around the cursor, or every echo in the text, between {{ }} and {!! !!}. */\r\nfunction toggleEcho(text, offset) {\r\n  const re = /\\{\\{(?!--)\\s*([\\s\\S]*?)\\s*\\}\\}|\\{!!\\s*([\\s\\S]*?)\\s*!!\\}/g;\r\n  let m;\r\n  while ((m = re.exec(text))) {\r\n    if (offset >= m.index && offset <= m.index + m[0].length) {\r\n      const raw = m[0].startsWith('{!!');\r\n      const inner = raw ? m[2] : m[1];\r\n      return { start: m.index, end: m.index + m[0].length, text: raw ? '{{ ' + inner + ' }}' : '{!! ' + inner + ' !!}', toRaw: !raw };\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  return null;\r\n}\r\n\r\nconst WRAPS = {\r\n  '@if': { open: (a) => '@if (' + (a || '$condition') + ')', close: '@endif' },\r\n  '@foreach': { open: (a) => '@foreach (' + (a || '$items as $item') + ')', close: '@endforeach' },\r\n  '@auth': { open: () => '@auth', close: '@endauth' },\r\n  '@guest': { open: () => '@guest', close: '@endguest' },\r\n  '@can': { open: (a) => \"@can('\" + (a || 'update') + \"', $model)\", close: '@endcan' },\r\n  '@isset': { open: (a) => '@isset(' + (a || '$variable') + ')', close: '@endisset' },\r\n  '@php': { open: () => '@php', close: '@endphp' },\r\n  '@push': { open: (a) => \"@push('\" + (a || 'scripts') + \"')\", close: '@endpush' },\r\n  '@section': { open: (a) => \"@section('\" + (a || 'content') + \"')\", close: '@endsection' },\r\n  '@error': { open: (a) => \"@error('\" + (a || 'field') + \"')\", close: '@enderror' },\r\n  '@env': { open: (a) => \"@env('\" + (a || 'local') + \"')\", close: '@endenv' },\r\n  '@once': { open: () => '@once', close: '@endonce' },\r\n};\r\n\r\nfunction wrap(selected, kind, arg, unit = '    ') {\r\n  const w = WRAPS[kind];\r\n  if (!w) throw new Error('Unknown directive ' + kind);\r\n  const lines = selected.replace(/\\r\\n/g, '\\n').replace(/\\n+$/, '').split('\\n');\r\n  const indent = (/^\\s*/.exec(lines[0]) || [''])[0];\r\n  return indent + w.open(arg) + '\\n' + lines.map((l) => (l.trim() ? unit + l : l)).join('\\n') + '\\n' + indent + w.close;\r\n}\r\n\r\n/** class=\"a b {{ $x ? 'c' : '' }}\" to @class(['a', 'b', 'c' => $x]) when the expression is a simple ternary or &&. */\r\nfunction classToDirective(attr) {\r\n  const m = /^class\\s*=\\s*\"([^\"]*)\"$/.exec(attr.trim());\r\n  if (!m) return null;\r\n  const parts = [];\r\n  const body = m[1];\r\n  const re = /\\{\\{\\s*(.+?)\\s*\\}\\}|([^\\s{]+)/g;\r\n  let x;\r\n  while ((x = re.exec(body))) {\r\n    if (x[2]) parts.push(\"'\" + x[2] + \"'\");\r\n    else {\r\n      const e = x[1];\r\n      let t = /^(.+?)\\s*\\?\\s*['\"]([^'\"]+)['\"]\\s*:\\s*['\"]{2}$/.exec(e);\r\n      if (t) {\r\n        parts.push(\"'\" + t[2] + \"' => \" + t[1].trim());\r\n        continue;\r\n      }\r\n      t = /^(.+?)\\s*&&\\s*['\"]([^'\"]+)['\"]$/.exec(e);\r\n      if (t) {\r\n        parts.push(\"'\" + t[2] + \"' => \" + t[1].trim());\r\n        continue;\r\n      }\r\n      return null;\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  return '@class([' + parts.join(', ') + '])';\r\n}\r\n\r\nconst kebab = (s) => s.replace(/([a-z0-9])([A-Z])/g, '$1-$2').replace(/[\\s_.]+/g, '-').toLowerCase();\r\n\r\n/** The variables a piece of markup uses, so a new component can declare them as props. */\r\nfunction usedVariables(markup) {\r\n  const names = new Set();\r\n  for (const m of markup.matchAll(/\\$([A-Za-z_]\\w*)/g)) names.add(m[1]);\r\n  for (const m of markup.matchAll(/@(?:foreach|forelse)\\s*\\([^)]*\\sas\\s+(?:\\$\\w+\\s*=>\\s*)?\\$(\\w+)\\)/g)) names.delete(m[1]);\r\n  names.delete('loop');\r\n  names.delete('slot');\r\n  names.delete('attributes');\r\n  return [...names];\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction componentSource(markup, props) {\r\n  const head = props.length ? '@props([' + props.map((p) => \"'\" + p + \"'\").join(', ') + '])\\n\\n' : '';\r\n  return head + markup.replace(/\\n+$/, '') + '\\n';\r\n}\r\n\r\nexports._test = { formatBlade, tidySpacing, toggleEcho, wrap, classToDirective, usedVariables, componentSource, kebab, tokens };\r\n\r\nexports.activate = function (context) {\r\n  async function replaceAll(doc, text) {\r\n    await ferrum.editor.replace({ start: { line: 0, col: 0 }, end: { line: doc.lineCount, col: 0 } }, text);\r\n  }\r\n  const unit = () => (ferrum.settings.get('laravelBlade.useTabs') === true ? '\\t' : ' '.repeat(Math.max(1, Math.min(8, Number(ferrum.settings.get('laravelBlade.indentSize')) || 4))));\r\n  const offsetOf = (doc) => {\r\n    const lines = doc.text.split('\\n');\r\n    let o = 0;\r\n    for (let i = 0; i < doc.selection.start.line; i++) o += lines[i].length + 1;\r\n    return o + doc.selection.start.col;\r\n  };\r\n  const root = () => ferrum.workspace.root;\r\n  const full = (p) => root() + (root().includes('\\\\') ? '\\\\' : '/') + p;\r\n\r\n  async function target() {\r\n    const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\r\n    if (!doc) ferrum.window.showMessage('Open a Blade file first.', 'warn');\r\n    return doc;\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  context.subscriptions.push(\r\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelBlade.format', async () => {\r\n      const doc = await target();\r\n      if (!doc) return;\r\n      let out = formatBlade(doc.text, unit());\r\n      if (ferrum.settings.get('laravelBlade.tidyEchoes') !== false) out = tidySpacing(out);\r\n      if (out === doc.text) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Already formatted.');\r\n      await replaceAll(doc, out);\r\n    }),\r\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelBlade.tidyEchoes', async () => {\r\n      const doc = await target();\r\n      if (!doc) return;\r\n      const out = tidySpacing(doc.selectedText || doc.text);\r\n      if (doc.selectedText) await ferrum.editor.insert(out);\r\n      else await replaceAll(doc, out);\r\n    }),\r\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelBlade.toggleEcho', async () => {\r\n      const doc = await target();\r\n      if (!doc) return;\r\n      const hit = toggleEcho(doc.text, offsetOf(doc));\r\n      if (!hit) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Put the cursor inside {{ ... }} or {!! ... !!}.', 'warn');\r\n      const pos = (o) => {\r\n        const before = doc.text.slice(0, o).split('\\n');\r\n        return { line: before.length - 1, col: before[before.length - 1].length };\r\n      };\r\n      await ferrum.editor.replace({ start: pos(hit.start), end: pos(hit.end) }, hit.text);\r\n      if (hit.toRaw) ferrum.window.showMessage('Unescaped output: make sure the value is trusted.', 'warn');\r\n    }),\r\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelBlade.wrap', async () => {\r\n      const doc = await target();\r\n      if (!doc) return;\r\n      if (!doc.selectedText) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Select the markup to wrap first.', 'warn');\r\n      const kind = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick(Object.keys(WRAPS).map((k) => ({ label: k })), { placeholder: 'Wrap the selection in...' });\r\n      if (!kind) return;\r\n      let arg = '';\r\n      if (['@if', '@foreach', '@can', '@isset', '@push', '@section', '@error', '@env'].includes(kind.label)) {\r\n        const a = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Argument', placeholder: { '@if': '$user->isAdmin()', '@foreach': '$posts as $post', '@can': 'update', '@isset': '$variable', '@push': 'scripts', '@section': 'content', '@error': 'email', '@env': 'local' }[kind.label] });\r\n        if (a === undefined) return;\r\n        arg = a;\r\n      }\r\n      await ferrum.editor.insert(wrap(doc.selectedText, kind.label, arg, unit()));\r\n    }),\r\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelBlade.classDirective', async () => {\r\n      const doc = await target();\r\n      if (!doc) return;\r\n      const attr = doc.selectedText || '';\r\n      const out = classToDirective(attr);\r\n      if (!out) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Select a class=\"...\" attribute whose {{ }} parts are simple conditions like {{ $on ? \\'active\\' : \\'\\' }}.', 'warn');\r\n      await ferrum.editor.insert(out);\r\n    }),\r\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelBlade.extractComponent', async () => {\r\n      const doc = await target();\r\n      if (!doc) return;\r\n      if (!doc.selectedText) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Select the markup to move out first.', 'warn');\r\n      if (!root()) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Open the project folder first.', 'warn');\r\n      const raw = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Component name', placeholder: 'alert  or  forms.input' });\r\n      if (!raw) return;\r\n      const parts = raw.split(/[./\\\\]/).filter(Boolean).map(kebab);\r\n      if (!parts.length || parts.some((p) => !/^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$/.test(p))) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Use letters, digits and dashes: alert, forms.input', 'error');\r\n      const props = usedVariables(doc.selectedText);\r\n      const path = full('resources/views/components/' + parts.join('/') + '.blade.php');\r\n      if (!(await ferrum.window.confirm('Create ' + 'resources/views/components/' + parts.join('/') + '.blade.php and replace the selection with <x-' + parts.join('.') + ' />?', 'Create'))) return;\r\n      await ferrum.workspace.writeFile(path, componentSource(doc.selectedText, props));\r\n      await ferrum.editor.insert('<x-' + parts.join('.') + (props.length ? ' ' + props.map((p) => ':' + p + '=\"$' + p + '\"').join(' ') : '') + ' />');\r\n    }),\r\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelBlade.extractPartial', async () => {\r\n      const doc = await target();\r\n      if (!doc) return;\r\n      if (!doc.selectedText) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Select the markup to move out first.', 'warn');\r\n      if (!root()) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Open the project folder first.', 'warn');\r\n      const raw = await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Partial view name', placeholder: 'partials.sidebar' });\r\n      if (!raw) return;\r\n      const parts = raw.split(/[./\\\\]/).filter(Boolean);\r\n      if (!parts.length || parts.some((p) => !/^[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$/.test(p))) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Use letters, digits, dashes and dots: partials.sidebar', 'error');\r\n      const props = usedVariables(doc.selectedText);\r\n      const path = full('resources/views/' + parts.join('/') + '.blade.php');\r\n      if (!(await ferrum.window.confirm('Create resources/views/' + parts.join('/') + '.blade.php and replace the selection with @include?', 'Create'))) return;\r\n      await ferrum.workspace.writeFile(path, doc.selectedText.replace(/\\n+$/, '') + '\\n');\r\n      await ferrum.editor.insert(\"@include('\" + parts.join('.') + \"'\" + (props.length ? ', [' + props.map((p) => \"'\" + p + \"' => $\" + p).join(', ') + ']' : '') + ')');\r\n    }),\r\n  );\r\n};\r\n\r\nexports.deactivate = function () {};\r\n"},"README.md":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"# Laravel Blade Tools\n\nWorks on files in the **Laravel Blade** language (install the Laravel Blade extension for colors).\n\n- **Format Blade File** (Ctrl+Alt+B) re-indents HTML tags and Blade directives together: `@if/@elseif/@else/@endif`, `@foreach`, `@forelse/@empty`, `@switch/@case`, `@section`, `@push`, `@auth`, `@can`, `@php ... @endphp`, `@slot`, `<x-...>` components and more. The inside of `<script>`, `<style>`, `<pre>` and `<textarea>` is left exactly as it is. One line directives such as `@section('title', 'Home')` and `@php(...)` do not indent.\n- **Tidy {{ }} Spacing** makes `{{$x}}` into `{{ $x }}` and `@if(` into `@if (`.\n- **Toggle {{ }} and {!! !!}** switches the echo under the cursor between escaped and raw. Raw output shows a warning.\n- **Wrap Selection in a Directive...** wraps the selected markup in `@if`, `@foreach`, `@auth`, `@guest`, `@can`, `@isset`, `@php`, `@push`, `@section`, `@error`, `@env` or `@once`, and indents it.\n- **Turn class=\"...\" into @class** converts `class=\"btn {{ $on ? 'active' : '' }}\"` to `@class(['btn', 'active' => $on])`.\n- **Extract Selection to a Blade Component...** creates `resources/views/components/name.blade.php` with an `@props` line for the variables it uses and replaces the selection with `<x-name :var=\"$var\" />`.\n- **Extract Selection to a Partial...** creates the view and writes `@include('partials.name', [...])`.\n\nThe two extract commands ask before they create a file. Permission: workspace.write.\n"}}}